  "notes": "Web 401 — LIVE-MILES-TRAIL-RECONCILE-NOV10 (owner Nov 10, 2026 09:47 CST: the cloud Manifest read 'GPS distance 27.2 km' from today's crumb trail while his phone's live counter read ~5 km — 'it's not on the live kilometers in the app'). Follow-on to web 399's cloud floor: the floor restores the tracker record's liveMilesM stamp, but his Nov 10 wipe (cache cleared 09:20, counter restarted at 0.2 km) predated any stamp, so the floor had nothing to give — while the day's whole distance stood in the synced GPS crumb trail the whole time. THE FIX (js/miles.js only): at the same two seams the floor uses (startDay, reseedFromStore/adoptFromStore), foldDayTrail joins the live session's day trail with the Manifest's own filing rule (every livemiles record, each crumb under its OWN timestamp's day, deduped t|a|o, time order — the v245 join adoptableFragments' record-date filing and the total-only reseed both miss), asks with the Manifest's own ruler (the consecutive chain sum) whether the trail covers MORE than the counter holds, and only then folds it through mergeCrumbs — the engine's own rebuild fold, whose counted-coverage (segs) dedupe books only uncounted ground, under the standing filters, with unobserved joins settling as bridges. It only ever raises; gates mirror the floor (session key only, tracker naming THIS session live within the v361 pin family, crumbs under the pin's own date — an idle/closed day and other sessions/days get nothing); folded metres are labelled trailFoldM on the day record (the bridgedM/cloudFloorM idiom, stamped + preserved in persist). Convicted by tools/live-miles-trail-reconcile-nov10-test.js (failing-first on live 400: T1/T2/T5 fail, counter stands at 0.21 km against a 27.6 km trail; 12/12 here); the miles family and every suite that loads miles.js at pristine-live standings. version.json from live 400: native 74 + meticulous-v74.apk preserved, webVersion 401; index pin js/miles.js 400 -> 401; files map refreshed for js/miles.js + index.html. Job A NOT in this release. IN-HANDS VERDICT OWED: on a day whose trail is already in the cloud, a wiped/young counter reconciles up to the trail figure on relaunch (and when a pull lands the trail mid-day) — the live miles match the Manifest's GPS distance instead of standing at a fraction of it.",
